' Question: what happens, in order, when the owner starts a Grid bot, and on which thread?
' Explained by: ../06-runtime.md, which cites each step. Drawn by hand, high level.
@startuml 06-start
participant "StartBotCommandHandler\n(caller's thread)" as UC
participant BotRunner as R
participant GridStartPreconditions as P
participant IBotStore as ST
participant "GridExecutor\n(bot's worker)" as G
participant GridStartSequence as S
participant trading as T

UC -> UC : refuse a closed venue, an unconfirmed\nMainnet start, an unready bot
UC -> R : start(bot_id)
R -> R : retire the earlier run's worker;\nDRAFT or STOPPED --start--> STARTING (not saved yet)
R -> P : check(bot)
P -> T : claim the symbol, open the order session,\nregister the owner budget
alt refused
  P --> UC : the refusal; nothing saved, nothing queued
else admitted
  R -> ST : save(STARTING)
  R -> G : start() (queued on a fresh worker)
  note over UC, R : the caller returns here
  G -> S : run(plan)
  S -> T : place the ladder, level by level
  S -> G : ladder_ready
  G -> G : STARTING --ladder_ready--> RUNNING
end
@enduml
